From da4bafb29646756a4f4ff75fb1b66c8c1fb45e63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nikuzo <buelaniki@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:29:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: new mtk-ccci plugin for MediaTek SoC modems

MediaTek SoC modems (MT6768 and friends) talk AT over CCCI character
devices and carry data on the ccmni network interfaces, but +CGACT
contexts are never bound to those interfaces. Follow the stock RIL
instead: allow data with AT+EDALLOW=1, activate the PDN with
AT+EAPNACT=1,"<apn>","default",0, take the ccmni the modem picked from
the +EIF: <id>, ifup URC (<id> % 100), confirm it with
AT+EIF=<id>,"ifst","up",<type>, find the PDN id and DNS servers with
+CGCONTRDP and its addresses with AT+EPDN=<id>,"addr" (static IPv4, IPv6
link-local for SLAAC), and deactivate it with AT+EAPNACT=0,<id>,0.

Every +EIF: <id>, ifdown must be confirmed with
AT+EIF=<id>,"ifst","down",0 as the stock NetAgent does, or the modem
keeps the interface reserved and runs out of them (+CME ERROR: 3843).

Ports are selected with the ID_MM_MTK_CCCI udev tag.
